 "verdict": "60 prompts x 8 raters detects a transport effect of +0.05 at 80% power, clustering on prompt. r12's observed drop is 0.16, which is detectable at every cell in this grid -- so the binding constraint on the human experiment is NOT statistical power. It is the sampling frame: with equal cells and weights, 30 prompts give both a population estimate and an anomaly-subset estimate from one collection, and without them an anomaly-selected sample would return a transport number that is really a number about the strangest prompts.",
 "note": "Power is clustered on PROMPT, not binomial on pairs: six comparisons from one rater's ranking of four responses are one object, and raters within a prompt share its difficulty. Surface distance only; representation distance from three backbones is G33 and is deliberately not done here."
}